# The drawer

When a `-#` hash note is swept it doesn't vanish — its prose moves here and a
`≡<hash>` handle is left at the anchor in the source. This `resource` is the
**drawer**: the queryable hot mirror of every collapsed note. The cold backstop
is git (the note was a real line once; `git show <hash>` recovers it), so a row
here is a convenience cache, never the sole copy.

The `hash` is the dereference spine — a short prefix of the sweep commit's sha
(`≡a3f9` ⇒ `git show a3f9`), suffixed when several notes collapse in one sweep.
`parent` carries the nesting: a rolled-up stack points its children at one parent
hash. See [[hash-notes]].

resource HashNote do
  hash :id
  file :text
  anchor :int
  text :text
  polarity :pin | :drawer
  state :live | :collapsed
  parent :text
  born_at :text
  swept_at :text
  author :text
end
